          "text": "I need implement FB_Task exact interface. Should have timing wall elapsed since previous invocation. No TIME input. Use TON standard with PT T#5S called each scan? Standard TON ET accumulates realtime between invocations and when IN false resets. Simplest: tonStart(IN := DO_LOW AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC, PT:=T#5S); BLOWER_RUN := tonStart.Q; count rising detection. Should have initial count zero explicit. At power up defaults. Timer ET zero first eligible invocation standard. Yes.\n\nPotential test harness uses fake time? CODESYS compile only. Use TON, R_TRIG perhaps. Implementation:\nfbStartDelay(IN := DO_LOW AND AERATION_E_STOP_NC, PT := T#5S);\nBLOWER_RUN := fbStartDelay.Q;\nfbRunEdge(CLK := BLOWER_RUN);\nIF fbRunEdge.Q THEN count := count +1; END_IF;\nOrdering immediate disable: TON invocation with false sets Q false same scan. Fine.\nAt powerup initialize output count zero using :=0. BLOWER_RUN := FALSE. Counting retains.\n\nPotential compiler library Standard available. TON in standard. Declaration include VAR fbStartDelay : TON; fbRunEdge : R_TRIG; END_VAR. Could avoid R_TRIG use prev bool initialized false. Simpler. IF BLOWER_RUN AND NOT xRunPrev THEN count + 1. xRunPrev := BLOWER_RUN. This avoids helper. Should have UINT addition literal 1 accepted. Use AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT := AERATION_BLOWER_CYCLE_COUNT + UINT#1; syntax UINT#1 valid. Usually + 1 fine.\n\nCompile."
